            "date": "2026-11-21T14:05:07+01:00"
          },
          "message": "fix(ui): keep trailing parts of list items right-aligned on wrap (#15093)\n\nIn issue lists, the trailing block (assignees, comment count, tracked time) is rendered at the left edge of its own line when the title and labels are long enough to fill the whole row. It should stay right-aligned like in rows where everything fits on one line.\n\n`.flex-item-header` uses `flex-wrap: wrap`. When the title and labels fill the row, `.flex-item-trailing` wraps onto a new line. It has `flex-grow: 0`, so it sits at the start of that line and `justify-content: end` has no effect. The fix adds `margin-inline-start: auto` to `.flex-item .flex-item-trailing`, which pushes it to the right in both cases.\n\nThe rule is in the shared `flex-list.css`, so it also applies to other lists that use `flex-item-trailing`. Rows where the trailing block does not wrap look the same as before.\n\nReviewed-on: https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo/pulls/15093\nReviewed-by: 0ko <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
